> Original eight-vertex graph

Retain0→1→2→0,3→4→5→3, the bridge2→3, and tail5→6→7. All vertices and directed
edges below are the original example. Labels are actual output, and each
displayed edge remains a directed input edge. The expected groups have
sizes3,3,1,1. Comparing group membership with mutual reachability is stronger
independent evidence than matching numeric labels from Tarjan, whose component
ordering can differ.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kosaraju_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<std::vector<int>> a = {{1}, {2}, {0, 3}, {4}, {5}, {3, 6},
                                             {7}, {}};
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::kosaraju_trace(8, a);
    std::print("| original vertex | actual SCC label | actual first-pass finish ordinal |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (int v = 0; v < 8; ++v) {
        const auto it =
            std::find(t.finish_order.begin(), t.finish_order.end(), v);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", v, t.component[v],
                   it - t.finish_order.begin());
    }
    const std::vector<std::array<double, 2>> pos = {{0, 4}, {5, 4}, {5, 0},
                                                    {10, 4}, {15, 4}, {15, 0},
                                                    {10, -4}, {5, -4}};
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (int v = 0; v < 8; ++v)
        d.node(std::to_string(v), {pos[v][0], pos[v][1]},
               std::format("Vertex {}\nSCC {}", v, t.component[v]));
    for (int u = 0; u < 8; ++u)
        for (int v : a[u])
            d.edge(std::to_string(u), std::to_string(v));
    d.save_svg("build/kosaraju_original.svg");
}
```
